  "id": "campgiardia",
  "note": "CAMP GIARDIA — a camp on the pond shore that has stopped being temporary.\n\nThe tile's prose: tarpaulin over a bus shell, a cook fire in a cut-down drum, a hand-lettered\nboard reading CAMP GIARDIA, and a row of beans along the waterline that something has eaten.\n\nSo the bus is the room: a long body sitting on its frame with the wheels gone, a row of windows\ndown each side and a door at one end. The tarp is thrown over the bus roof and carried forward on\ntwo poles, so there is a dry yard along the side. The far end of the bus sticks out from under it,\nbecause a tarp that hid the whole bus made the camp a beige slab from any height. The cook fire is\na drum in the open at that end. The\nboard stands on two posts at the road. The bean canes run along the back, by the water.\n\nNothing is lit but the bus windows and the fire.\n\nIt stands in for the `campgiardia` arm (`replaces`), which stays in LEGACY_MODELS.",
  "pal": "ty_giardia_bus",
